{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/924791-demon-the-fallen-question-lores-above-5-dots","id":924791,"title":"Demon The Fallen question..... Lores above 5 Dots?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-01T23:49:02-07:00","id":924791,"title":"Demon The Fallen question..... Lores above 5 Dots?","content":"I'm currently running a DtF game and my next session I've planned on having the characters enter a fugue state together as discussed on page 63 in the Demon The Fallen Player's Guide.<br /> <br /> What I had planned was have them go back completely into their memories of a major battle and during that time I wanted their character's to be quite powerful for the fight I plan to put them in. I was wondering if there is anywhere in the Dtf books that discuss lore dots going past 5? I'm willing to make them up if need be I just needed some guidance if anyone had any ideas. If you want me to be specific please ask any probing questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7264-sawrunner8","name":"SAWrunner8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7264_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T07:51:41-07:00","id":924883,"title":"","content":"It was mentioned somewhere, but only to the degree of &quot;if lores of level 6+ exist , they must truly be rare and earthshatteringly powerful.&quot; personally I would boost the characters faith and lore dicepools for the fugue and on top of that give them mastery. 3-5 dots of mastery are quite enough to cause widefelt destruction, so that definitly fits the description.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T15:38:12-07:00","id":925073,"title":"","content":"Alright I'll do that then. If anyone does find any info on Level 6+ lores please tell me. One of my characters I did intend to be the eldest and more powerful than the others. Talking Baron level powerful during that time. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7264-sawrunner8","name":"SAWrunner8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7264_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T16:29:47-07:00","id":925092,"title":"","content":"unfortunately lores level 6+ do not exist. that's why mastery exists instead","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T12:29:36-07:00","id":925457,"title":"","content":"Personally, i think it would be Way too game breaking (like the spheres level 6 to 10)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T21:14:15-07:00","id":925686,"title":"","content":"Didn't they give some of Belial's statistics in an explanation of how Mastery works? I'd say if the most powerful of the Archdukes of Hell doesn't break the 5-dot cap, doing so isn't a thing that would be available to any PCs. Unless someone's playing Lucifer or an unfallen archangel in your game, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T08:34:36-07:00","id":925913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/924791-demon-the-fallen-question-lores-above-5-dots?p=925686#post925686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't they give some of Belial's statistics in an explanation of how Mastery works? I'd say if the most powerful of the Archdukes of Hell doesn't break the 5-dot cap, doing so isn't a thing that would be available to any PCs. Unless someone's playing Lucifer or an unfallen archangel in your game, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say lucy himself probably only sticks to lore 5/mastery 5, only he knows all lores 5(except earthbound lores. he deeply hates them and everything they represent in cannon, so I don't see him destroying reality in an area or eating human souls) and his apocolyptic form has unique abilities. The only real difference I can disseminate from the fluff between an eloheim and a fallen is the fact that eloheim have unlimited faith and don't suffer from torment(Which in game I run as them having a faith-pool of 20 that refreshes every round).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T09:57:44-07:00","id":925941,"title":"","content":"And even then, an elohim needs to be in the good graces of God to have unlimited faith, after all, Lucifer himself was captured when his forces stopped receiving huge amounts of Faith after the Babel fiasco.<br /> <br /> However, I personaly preffer to not give concrete powers and limits to Archdukes and beyond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T05:31:16-07:00","id":926367,"title":"","content":"Where would I find the rules for mastery? Sounds interesting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: Nevermind, found it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":945,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/945-space-monkey","user":"Space Monkey","date":". 07-05-2016, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/945-space-monkey","name":"Space Monkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T16:01:09-07:00","id":927814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/924791-demon-the-fallen-question-lores-above-5-dots?p=925941#post925941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even then, an elohim needs to be in the good graces of God to have unlimited faith, after all, Lucifer himself was captured when his forces stopped receiving huge amounts of Faith after the Babel fiasco.<br /> <br /> However, I personaly preffer to not give concrete powers and limits to Archdukes and beyond.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh, I like doing it. It's fun when a player does something unexpected that screws with the cannon, like killing asmodeus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}